WEBVTT

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:36.410
The monster king of the world of
darkness is the Dark Lord Shabranigdo.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.820
This Dark Lord, who
still sleeps in the far north...

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:42.360
...created five high-ranking
Monsters from himself.

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:47.750
Among them, the one who loves war
most is Gaav, the Demon Dragon King...

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:51.130
...who's the ringleader behind what
happened in Atlas City and Seyruun.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.400
We can't just stand
by and let him do this.

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.400
So, my friends and I are off on a
new journey to find a magic power...

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.370
...which can stand up
to a high-level Monster.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.850
Hmm..."Welcome to Rikido village..."

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:22.450
"Throw a coin in the
fountain and ring the bell..."

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:25.430
"...and good things will happen.
The Rikido Tourist Board."

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:28.370
Their economy must be in a slump...

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:36.370
Look, I don't mind traveling around
looking for a Claire Bible manuscript...

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.570
...but why can't we find
a decent copy of one?!

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.910
All we find are things with weird
dance steps, phony detectors...

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.850
...and stuff that sorta SOUNDS
like the Claire Bible!

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.120
Nothing but useless things.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:52.390
Ooh... Isn't there a real copy
of the thing ANYWHERE?!

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:57.260
Are you saying you'd rather go
looking for the original Claire Bible?

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:00.100
You couldn't find something
like that very easily, right?

00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:02.070
I'm afraid that's right...

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:04.700
And when Gourry can call a
situation right, I feel even worse!

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:06.260
Really?

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.170
This may or may
not be helpful, but...

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.300
Well, you see, if you're
looking for a real manuscript...

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.410
A totally complete
copy of the Claire Bible...

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.850
...it's in a temple on
that mountain there.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.090
Why, you!
You've known that, and!

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:26.890
Yeah! Why didn't you
tell us this sooner?!

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.950
I didn't think it would
be of any use to you!

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.290
Meaning what?! Meaning what?!

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.730
Well, you see...

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.100
What are you doing?! Huh?

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.700
Are you all right, Master Xellos?!

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.370
Yes... I think.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.040
M- Martina?!

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.880
Why are you dressed like that?
What are you doing?

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:48.250
What do you mean "what"?
It's obvious, isn't it?

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:51.180
I have a part-time job to
earn my traveling money.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:52.950
Oh... Looks hard.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:55.120
Dammit, Part-Timer!

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.060
Quit goofing off
or you won't get paid!

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:58.590
Y- Yes, sir!

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:02.830
Hey, Martina, I hate to say this, but...
Your dress is wide open in back!

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.200
You tricked me...

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:09.970
You idiot!

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.900
Oh, I'm sorry, sir!

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:14.070
Why did I hire you?!

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.270
Come over here for a minute.

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.840
But it wasn't my fault!

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:20.850
That'll teach her to go hitting me.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.890
There you go, as always, being a
scary person who just makes enemies.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:26.990
Anyway, why don't we
go to this temple that...

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.820
...has this totally complete
copy of the Claire Bible?

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:43.400
"Here is stored a complete
copy of the Claire Bible..."

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:46.960
"...which contains limitless
knowledge from ancient times."

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:49.140
It's for real...

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:52.150
I still don't think this
will be of any use to you.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.030
Nice weather in here.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.590
How can this be
inside a building?

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:13.100
It looks like we
entered another dimension.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:15.730
Well? Where's the manuscript?

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.470
I'll show you in a minute.

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:38.390
This is...

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:39.760
...a totally complete...

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.730
...Claire Bible manuscript!

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:47.260
Just how is this not of any use
to us? This is great!

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:50.640
If the text it holds is complete,
we'll have no complaints.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:52.800
Oh, it's complete, I assure you.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:55.670
The trouble, of course,
is actually READING it.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.450
This isn't writing!

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:03.180
What?!

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:20.140
What's going on here?

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.640
Since they were trying to create...

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:25.670
...a complete copy of the
Claire Bible's limitless knowledge...

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:29.440
...they ended up creating a
limitless number of lithographs of it.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:33.110
Even then, the contents are in code,
so you can't read it easily.

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:35.710
And even if you find a way
to actually read the code...

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:38.720
...you have to find
the right ONE to read.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:41.780
How long do you think it'll take
to find the information you want?

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.820
If you're lucky, you'll find it soon.

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:48.630
If you're NOT lucky, you can spend
an entire lifetime and never find it!

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:53.970
Yeah, you're right... So, that's
how it works... Let's give it a try!

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:58.170
All we have to do is
find the tablet that says...

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.470
...how to beat any Monster in the
world and then decode it, right?!

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:09.150
It looks like this weird code can
affect the compass's movement.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:13.480
Long and short amounts of that
power may express some sort of words...

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:16.490
Maybe... Amelia,
have you found anything?

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.690
At the moment... Huh?

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:25.330
Ooh, if only I could find
just one keyword!

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:29.360
There is no form of code that
doesn't have meaning to somebody.

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:32.300
I'm sure there must
be a way to decipher it.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:41.650
Miss Lina! I can see
an old woman out there!

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.090
There's nobody out there!

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.590
I know I saw her, but...

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:56.600
There may be ghosts
haunting this strange place.

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:58.030
Please don't say that!

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:00.730
Oh, you think so?

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:07.570
Oh, did I scare you?
So sorry about that.

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:12.510
Oh, my!

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:18.510
So, who are you all?

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:21.520
People who need the
knowledge of the manuscript?

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:24.620
Yes, we definitely have a
use for the manuscript, but...

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:27.460
Well, you must have been surprised!

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:29.690
Especially when you saw
how many tablets there are!

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:31.760
Quite a problem, eh?

00:08:33.670 --> 00:08:35.160
So, lady, who are you?

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:41.700
Me? I'm Auntie Aqua,
the caretaker of the manuscript.

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:44.810
Auntie...

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.110
...Aqua?

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:56.120
So, how does this feel?

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:59.650
Ah, that's got it...

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:03.630
So, Auntie, you said you were
the manuscript's caretaker.

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:07.900
Does that mean you can understand
what's written on these things?

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:10.370
Oh, yes, of course.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.960
REALLY?!

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:16.170
So, can you lead us to the part of
the manuscript we're looking for?!

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:20.940
Yes, of course.
That's my job here, after all.

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:22.280
All right!

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:25.790
So, what is it you
people want to know?

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:28.950
Simple! We want to know a method
to fight the highest-level Monsters!

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:33.260
Hm? What did you say?

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:34.730
You can't help us?

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:39.000
Oh, it's not that. But if you
want to have that knowledge...

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:42.600
...you'll need three
days worth of food.

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:45.200
Three days worth of food?

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.400
What would we need that for?

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:52.310
Because the manuscript
with the knowledge you seek...

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:55.820
...is a three-day journey from here.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.610
It's THAT far away?!

00:09:57.690 --> 00:10:00.120
Well, this is
a complete manuscript...

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:03.120
...of the limitless
knowledge of the Claire Bible.

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.490
I see...

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.120
Well, then, let's get that food!

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:06.850
Right!

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:08.020
All right!

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:10.620
Food! Food! Food!

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.540
So, they're in the
manuscript shrine, eh?

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:28.210
Yes...

00:10:28.280 --> 00:10:31.250
Even Xellos must be
getting excited now...

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:39.160
This is three-days
worth of food for you?!

00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:40.700
Yeah, well, basically...

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:43.990
If we didn't have enough,
Lina would probably eat the camels.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:45.920
WHO would eat them?!

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:49.360
Would you stop talking
like idiots? Let's go!

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:52.370
Hey, hold on!
You're so impatient...

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:54.870
Hey, Auntie...

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:59.310
This is a fine way to take an old
lady like me on a trip like this.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:26.970
I see. So, the Demon Dragon
King Gaav is after you.

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:28.710
That must be awful!

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:29.980
Oh, it's all right.

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:33.350
But, like I said, I can't just
stand around doing nothing.

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:38.080
Well, it's not like I have nothing to
use against him if things get desperate.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:39.290
Oh?

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:40.990
Yeah...

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:45.460
The Dark Lord who rules
over all other Dark Lords...

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:47.700
The Lord of Nightmares...

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.740
The forbidden spell
of ultimate power.

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:54.940
If that power should
go out of control...

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:59.540
...it could endanger
the entire world.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:04.510
The thing is, I want to try and
find a slightly safer method...

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:08.050
...before I resort to something
as dangerous as THAT.

00:12:08.690 --> 00:12:10.180
I see...

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:13.320
But you seem to know all about
Gaav, the Demon Dragon King, Auntie.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:14.860
O- Oh, do I?

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:17.900
Well, it's only natural that
I'd remember a few things like that...

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:21.160
...considering how long I've been
caring for these manuscripts.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.770
Hmm... Is that it?

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:26.870
Those two seem to have
made friends quickly.

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:30.440
Lina's a lot nicer person
than she sometimes seems.

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:36.650
Lina, I can carry
her if you get tired.

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.910
Don't worry about it.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:44.620
Oh, by the way, that
man with the long hair...

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:47.420
You mean Gourry?

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:49.790
Just what is your
relationship with him?

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:55.830
Huh?! Wha...
Uh, r- relationship? Well, uh...

00:12:56.610 --> 00:12:57.940
Is he important to you?

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.100
Come on, Auntie! Cut it out!

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:04.080
He's just some guy I can't get rid
of who says he's my protector!

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:06.050
Oh, I see. I see...

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:08.310
Could we just drop
the subject, please?

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:23.190
Just who is that old woman?

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:27.360
She doesn't seem to be one of
Gaav's Monsters in disguise, but...

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:30.830
Why did they leave me behind?!

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.340
They're not gonna get
rid of me THAT easily!

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:42.650
Oh, Monstrous Zoamelgustar!
Please guide me!

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:46.990
Wait for me, Master Xellos!
Your Martina is coming to you now!

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:48.820
This way!

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:55.020
Ah, that hits the spot!

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:57.220
So, night falls in here as well.

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:01.430
It looks that way.

00:14:03.210 --> 00:14:04.640
Isn't it pretty?

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.300
Amelia...

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:12.140
That was scary!

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:14.180
Hm? What are yelling about?

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:20.320
Gourry?

00:14:20.390 --> 00:14:21.910
Oh, are you up?

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:24.390
Good for you!
You were standing guard?

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.930
Yeah. I switched off with Zel.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:29.560
Come over here. The night
gets pretty cold in here.

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:31.150
Oh, sure.

00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:35.800
Want some?

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:37.200
No thanks!

00:14:42.110 --> 00:14:46.880
By the way... We've been traveling
together for a while, haven't we?

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.740
Oh? Has it been that long?

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:57.720
It just... It seems so natural
to think of you being with me.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:00.760
Well, I am your
protector, after all.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:04.360
And, well... How long do
you plan on protecting me?

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:07.830
I dunno...
The rest of my life?

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:11.270
The rest of?!

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:14.640
Oh, man! What am I doing?!

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:17.680
What that old lady said
has me acting totally weird!

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:24.250
Gourry... Don't you have
somebody waiting for you?

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:27.290
Somebody... you really like?

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:49.310
Miss Lina?

00:15:50.350 --> 00:15:52.710
A-A-Auntie!

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:54.010
Come with me, won't you?

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:04.360
C'mon, what do you want?
I need my beauty sleep, you know.

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:06.020
Never mind that. Just come along.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:17.030
"Black tablet which carries forth
my will! Answer to my call!"

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:29.150
There. This is the
manuscript you wanted.

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:30.950
This is...

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:33.890
Try touching the
manuscript like this.

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:59.270
This place... I remember this place...

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:04.120
Shabranigdo?!

00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:10.480
Gourry! Amelia! Zel! And me?

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:13.090
What is this?

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:17.260
It is another past,
one of many possible ones.

00:17:17.330 --> 00:17:18.990
Another past?

00:17:27.110 --> 00:17:31.640
Let's go, Shabranigdo!
I'll bet everything on the Giga Slave!

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:38.210
"Darkness beyond the blackest pitch,
deeper than the deepest night!"

00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:44.050
"King of Darkness, who shines
like gold upon the Sea of Chaos!"

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:50.300
"I call upon thee!
Swear myself to thee!"

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:53.770
"Let the fools who stand
before me be destroyed..."

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:57.860
"...by the power
you and I possess!"

00:17:58.310 --> 00:18:00.970
Sword! Accept this darkness
and obey my command!

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:04.770
GIGA SLAVE!!!

00:18:22.970 --> 00:18:24.330
Miss Lina!

00:18:25.570 --> 00:18:26.500
Amelia!

00:18:28.470 --> 00:18:29.870
Zel!

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.400
Lina... save yourself!

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.000
Lina... Li...

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:44.580
Gourry! Gourry!! GOURRY!!!

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:05.370
What you just saw was
an out of control Giga Slave.

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:08.530
The Claire Bible showed you how
that battle might have ended.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:13.710
Why... Why did
you show me this?

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:19.220
Even I cannot know what
fate lies in store for you all.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:24.890
But you must avoid using
the Giga Slave at any cost!

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:28.550
You will soon face an enemy who,
while human in form...

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:33.470
...is stronger in battle
than any mere man.

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:36.800
When that happens, you will
have few options open to you.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:42.310
But you must be sure not
to make the wrong choice!

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:44.900
Because, if you do...

00:19:45.550 --> 00:19:49.240
Then why don't I just kill you
now and spare you the problem?!

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:52.450
Xellos?!

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:53.820
We can talk later!

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:58.420
So, you interfere yet again, Xellos!

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:00.690
Well, yes.
Of course, Mr. Saygram.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:05.990
Saygram?!

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:08.300
One of Gaav's servants?

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:11.310
It's been a long time.
What do want with us today?

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:14.780
To take all your lives, of course.

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:17.570
You've become a bit
of a nuisance for us!

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:20.010
Oh, my. Those aren't the sort
of words I expect to hear...

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:23.480
...from someone who turned
tail and ran like a coward!

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:27.050
Don't assume that I will
be the one fighting you.

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:30.050
Your opponent... shall be HIM!

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:35.790
It's been a long time, Xellos...

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.190
You!

00:20:40.270 --> 00:20:42.430
Yes, it's me! Gaav,
the Demon Dragon King!

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:45.060
G- Gaav, the Demon Dragon King?!

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:53.840
I've been shown what will happen
if I lose control of the Giga Slave.

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:56.510
But, with that sight
still echoing in my mind...

00:20:56.590 --> 00:20:59.350
...Gaav, the Demon
Dragon King, has appeared!

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:02.390
It looks like things have just
gotten a whole lot harder for us!
